          "title": "You'll want to know: xuéxí",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xuéxí — \"to study; to learn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ xuéxí hànyǔ — I'm learning Chinese."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xuéxí is built from 学 'to learn' and xí 'to practise', both inherited from Middle Chinese, haewk and zip (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary glosses zip with the first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking politely."
